# The ledger of `sql/build`: queries as values, measured against the yardstick
# the author named on 2026-11-16, which is no standard library: Go's
# `github.com/Masterminds/squirrel` v1.5.4 and `github.com/doug-martin/goqu/v9` v9.25.0
# (with `goqu/v9/exp`), `go doc -all` on each in a module of the scratch
# folder; Rust's `sea-query` 1.0.2, its item list on docs.rs; and Python's
# SQLAlchemy 2.1.8 Core, `dir()` of its modules installed in the scratch
# folder, counted as capabilities and not entry by entry, as the author asked.
# Every entry of squirrel and goqu that builds or renders SQL stands in a
# block; what runs a statement, scans into a struct or configures a global
# stands in `dropped`. Expected texts were written by hand from PostgreSQL's
# and SQLite's documentation and set beside SQLAlchemy's own rendering of the
# same queries (`compile` with `paramstyle` `numeric_dollar` and `numeric`),
# then run live on 2026-11-17 against this Mac's SQLite and PostgreSQL 16.15 (the
# drivers' tests, PostgreSQL's where `REBEL_POSTGRES_URL` names a server).

capability build/select  a SELECT made as a value: its columns and its table
  heroes  sql/build.select, sql/build.Select, sql/build.to_sql
  go      squirrel.Select, squirrel.SelectBuilder.Columns, squirrel.SelectBuilder.Column, squirrel.SelectBuilder.From, squirrel.StatementBuilder, squirrel.StatementBuilderType.Select, goqu.From, goqu.Select, goqu.SelectDataset.Select, goqu.SelectDataset.SelectAppend, goqu.SelectDataset.From, goqu.Star, goqu.S, goqu.T
  rust    sea_query::Query::select, SelectStatement::column, SelectStatement::columns, SelectStatement::from, SelectStatement::expr, Asterisk
  python  sqlalchemy.select, Select.add_columns, Select.with_only_columns, Select.select_from, sqlalchemy.table, sqlalchemy.column, Table.c

capability build/select-no-table  a SELECT of expressions alone, with no FROM
  heroes  sql/build.Select (`from` set to `[]`)
  go      squirrel.Select with no From, goqu.Select
  rust    SelectStatement with no from
  python  sqlalchemy.select of literals

