capability build/and-or-not  conditions combined: all hold, one holds, it does not hold
  heroes  sql/build.all_of, sql/build.any_of, sql/build.negate
  go      squirrel.And, squirrel.Or, goqu.And, goqu.Or, goqu.Ex, goqu.ExOr, exp.Ex, exp.ExOr, exp.ExpressionList, exp.NewExpressionList, exp.ExpressionListType, exp.BooleanExpression, exp.NewBooleanExpression, exp.BooleanOperation
  rust    Condition::all, Condition::any, Condition::not, all!, any!, ConditionHolder, ConditionHolderContents, ConditionType, LogicalChainOper, UnOper
  python  sqlalchemy.and_, sqlalchemy.or_, sqlalchemy.not_, sqlalchemy.true, sqlalchemy.false
  note    `AND` binds closer than `OR` in SQL; every combined part is put in parentheses here, so the text reads as the program wrote it

capability build/compare  a value compared: equal, not equal, less, greater, and their or-equal
  heroes  sql/build.equal, sql/build.not_equal, sql/build.less, sql/build.less_or_equal, sql/build.greater, sql/build.greater_or_equal
  go      squirrel.Eq, squirrel.NotEq, squirrel.Lt, squirrel.LtOrEq, squirrel.Gt, squirrel.GtOrEq, goqu.Ex, exp.Comparable.Eq, exp.Comparable.Neq, exp.Comparable.Gt, exp.Comparable.Gte, exp.Comparable.Lt, exp.Comparable.Lte, exp.Op
  rust    Expr::eq, Expr::ne, Expr::lt, Expr::lte, Expr::gt, Expr::gte, Expr::equals, BinOper
  python  ColumnOperators.__eq__, __ne__, __lt__, __le__, __gt__, __ge__, ColumnOperators.op, sqlalchemy.bindparam, sqlalchemy.literal
  note    the value is always a parameter; squirrel's Eq with a nil writes IS NULL, and so does `equal` here with `NULL`, since `= NULL` is never true. A `NULL` given to `<`, `<=`, `>`, `>=`, `LIKE` or `BETWEEN` is refused `invalid`: such a condition holds for no row

capability build/compare-columns  two columns or two expressions compared
  heroes  sql/build.columns_equal, sql/build.compare, sql/build.Op
  go      goqu.C(...).Eq(goqu.C(...)), squirrel.Expr
  rust    Expr::col(...).equals(...)
  python  table.c.a == other.c.b

capability build/in-list  a value among a list, or not
  heroes  sql/build.in_values
  go      squirrel.Eq with a slice, squirrel.NotEq with a slice, exp.Inable.In, exp.Inable.NotIn
  rust    Expr::is_in, Expr::is_not_in
  python  ColumnOperators.in_, ColumnOperators.not_in
  note    NOT IN is `negate` over `in_values`. An empty list holds for no row, written `1 = 0` since PostgreSQL refuses `IN ()`, and under `negate` for every row; SQLAlchemy writes an empty set the same way in other words. A NULL in the list is refused: it matches nothing, and under NOT it makes the condition hold for no row

capability build/in-query  a value among a subquery's rows, and a subquery that answers a row
  heroes  sql/build.in_query, sql/build.exists
  go      goqu.SelectDataset.Exists, goqu.Exists, exp.Inable.In with a dataset
  rust    Expr::in_subquery, Expr::not_in_subquery, Expr::exists, SubQueryOper, SubQueryStatement
  python  sqlalchemy.exists, ColumnOperators.in_ with a select, Select.exists

