capability build/like  text matched by a pattern, and a text matched as itself
  heroes  sql/build.like, sql/build.escape_like, sql/build.Op (`.like`, `.other`)
  go      squirrel.Like, squirrel.NotLike, squirrel.ILike, squirrel.NotILike, exp.Likeable.Like, exp.Likeable.NotLike, exp.Likeable.ILike, exp.Likeable.NotILike
  rust    Expr::like, Expr::not_like, LikeExpr, LikeExpr::escape
  python  ColumnOperators.like, not_like, ilike, not_ilike, contains, startswith, endswith, the `escape` and `autoescape` arguments
  note    every LIKE names its escape, a backslash, as a parameter: PostgreSQL's default escape is a backslash and SQLite has none, and a `'\'` in the text would mean another thing where `standard_conforming_strings` is off. ILIKE is PostgreSQL's and is written with `compare` and `.other`

capability build/regex  text matched by a regular expression
  heroes  sql/build.compare with `.other`
  go      exp.Likeable.RegexpLike, RegexpNotLike, RegexpILike, RegexpNotILike
  rust    PgBinOper::Matches, SqliteBinOper::Match, SqliteBinOper::Glob
  python  ColumnOperators.regexp_match, regexp_replace
  note    the operator is the database's own (`~` for PostgreSQL; SQLite's `REGEXP` needs a function the program registers), so it is written with `compare` and `.other`

