capability build/render  a query written as its text and its parameters
  heroes  sql/build.to_sql, sql/build.Statement
  go      squirrel.SelectBuilder.ToSql, MustSql, squirrel.InsertBuilder.ToSql, MustSql, squirrel.UpdateBuilder.ToSql, MustSql, squirrel.DeleteBuilder.ToSql, MustSql, squirrel.CaseBuilder.ToSql, MustSql, squirrel.Sqlizer, squirrel.And.ToSql, squirrel.Or.ToSql, squirrel.Eq.ToSql, squirrel.NotEq.ToSql, squirrel.Lt.ToSql, squirrel.LtOrEq.ToSql, squirrel.Gt.ToSql, squirrel.GtOrEq.ToSql, squirrel.Like.ToSql, squirrel.NotLike.ToSql, squirrel.ILike.ToSql, squirrel.NotILike.ToSql, goqu.SelectDataset.ToSQL, AppendSQL, goqu.InsertDataset.ToSQL, goqu.UpdateDataset.ToSQL, goqu.DeleteDataset.ToSQL, goqu.SelectDataset.Error, SetError, exp.SQLExpression, exp.AppendableExpression
  rust    SelectStatement::build, InsertStatement::build, UpdateStatement::build, DeleteStatement::build, QueryStatementBuilder, QueryStatementWriter
  python  ClauseElement.compile, Compiled.params, Compiled.string
  note    the text and the list of values a driver's `exec` and `query` take; a mistake in a query (a column with no name, a row of the wrong length) is a failure of this call, where squirrel and goqu keep it in the builder until ToSql

capability build/inline-values  a statement written with its values inside its text
  heroes  refused: a value inside the text is what this package exists to prevent; the text and `params` side by side show the same, and `sql/migrate.format_plan` writes them for a person
  go      squirrel.DebugSqlizer, goqu.L, goqu.Literal, goqu.V, goqu's non-prepared mode, exp.LiteralExpression, exp.NewLiteralExpression
  rust    SelectStatement::to_string, prepare::inject_parameters, raw_sql::seaql::debug, DebugQuery
  python  `compile_kwargs={"literal_binds": True}`, sqlalchemy.literal_column, alembic's inline_literal

capability build/raw  a fragment of SQL the builder does not offer
  heroes  sql/build.raw_without_values, sql/build.holds
  go      squirrel.Expr, squirrel.SelectBuilder.Prefix, PrefixExpr, Suffix, SuffixExpr, Options, the same on InsertBuilder, UpdateBuilder and DeleteBuilder, goqu.L, goqu.Literal
  rust    Expr::cust, Expr::cust_with_values, raw_query!, raw_sql!, RawSqlQueryBuilder, raw_sql::seaql::query
  python  sqlalchemy.text, sqlalchemy.literal_column, Select.prefix_with, Select.suffix_with
  note    the three take values into a fragment; here a fragment holds no value, and a quote, a semicolon, a comment, a `?` or a `$` in it fails `invalid`

capability build/row-to-record  a row read into a record, the columns named by its fields
  heroes  sql.text_named, sql.integer_named and the other reads of `sql` by name, given `Record::field` (spec § 9); sql/build.columns_named names the same fields as the columns
  go      goqu.SelectDataset.ScanStruct, ScanStructs, ScanVal, ScanVals, Pluck, ScanStructContext, ScanStructsContext, ScanValContext, ScanValsContext, PluckContext, squirrel.Row.Scan, squirrel.RowScanner
  rust    -
  python  Row._mapping, Row._asdict
  note    the field names come from `Record::field`, which the compiler checks (spec § 9); goqu reads a struct's tags by reflection at run time

capability build/record-to-row  a record's fields written as the columns and values of an INSERT
  heroes  refused: reading a record's fields at run time is reflection, which the language does not have; a program lists `[User::name, User::email]` and their values, which the compiler checks
  go      exp.NewRecordFromStruct, goqu.Insert with a struct, goqu.Update with a struct, goqu.SetIgnoreUntaggedFields, goqu.SetColumnRenameFunction
  rust    -
  python  -

capability build/orm  objects mapped to tables, tracked and saved: a session, an identity map, relations loaded when read
  heroes  refused: objects tracked and saved, an identity map and relations loaded when read need reflection (refused) and objects shared between places, and every value here is a copy; a program reads rows into records with `sql`'s reads by `Record::field` and writes them with `insert` and `update`
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  sqlalchemy.orm (Session, Mapped, mapped_column, relationship, DeclarativeBase, selectinload, joinedload), outside SQLAlchemy Core

capability build/schema  tables, indexes and keys made, changed and dropped as values (DDL)
  heroes  refused: a table is made by a migration's SQL in the database's own words (`sql/migrate`); DDL as values would be a second language for what each database writes differently
  go      -
  rust    Table::create, Table::alter, Table::drop, Table::rename, TableCreateStatement, TableAlterStatement, TableDropStatement, TableRenameStatement, ColumnDef, ColumnType, Index, IndexCreateStatement, IndexDropStatement, ForeignKey, ForeignKeyCreateStatement, ForeignKeyDropStatement, ForeignKeyAction, Check, TableOpt, TableAlterOption, TableDropOpt, StringLen, PartitionBy, PartitionValues, Type, TypeCreateStatement, TypeAlterStatement, TypeDropStatement, Extension, ExtensionCreateStatement, ExtensionDropStatement
  python  sqlalchemy.MetaData, Table, Column, Index, ForeignKey, ForeignKeyConstraint, PrimaryKeyConstraint, UniqueConstraint, CheckConstraint, Sequence, schema.CreateTable, schema.DropTable, schema.CreateIndex, schema.DropIndex, types

capability build/run  a built statement run on a connection
  heroes  refused: the package names no driver; `Statement.text` and `params` go to the driver's `exec` and `query` as they are
  go      squirrel.SelectBuilder.RunWith, Exec, ExecContext, Query, QueryContext, QueryRow, QueryRowContext, Scan, ScanContext, the same on InsertBuilder, UpdateBuilder and DeleteBuilder, squirrel.ExecWith, ExecContextWith, QueryWith, QueryContextWith, QueryRowWith, QueryRowContextWith, squirrel.BaseRunner, Runner, RunnerContext, StdSql, StdSqlCtx, WrapStdSql, WrapStdSqlCtx, Execer, ExecerContext, Queryer, QueryerContext, QueryRower, QueryRowerContext, Preparer, PreparerContext, DBProxy, DBProxyBeginner, DBProxyContext, goqu.New, goqu.Database, goqu.SQLDatabase, goqu.TxDatabase, goqu.NewTx, goqu.SQLTx, goqu.SelectDataset.Executor, Count, CountContext, goqu.InsertDataset.Executor, goqu.UpdateDataset.Executor, goqu.DeleteDataset.Executor
  rust    sqlx::query, sqlx::query_as (sea-query's sqlx feature)
  python  Connection.execute, Engine.connect

capability build/statement-cache  prepared statements kept and run again by their text
  heroes  refused: a connection's own: `sql/sqlite` keeps the statements it compiled, and every driver's `prepare` keeps one
  go      squirrel.StmtCache, squirrel.NewStmtCache, squirrel.NewStmtCacheProxy, squirrel.NewStmtCacher, squirrel.StmtCache.Clear, Exec, ExecContext, Prepare, PrepareContext, Query, QueryContext, QueryRow, QueryRowContext
  rust    -
  python  the compiled cache of an Engine

capability build/explain  a statement's plan asked for, EXPLAIN
  heroes  refused: the plan's form is each database's own; `EXPLAIN ` before `to_sql`'s text, which holds no value, asks it
  go      -
  rust    ExplainStatement, ExplainFormat, ExplainableStatement, PgExplainSerialize
  python  -

dropped
  go      goqu.SelectDataset.Clone, GetClauses, Expression, ReturnsColumns, GetAs, goqu.InsertDataset.Clone, GetClauses, Expression, ReturnsColumns, GetAs, goqu.UpdateDataset.Clone, GetClauses, Expression, ReturnsColumns, GetAs, goqu.DeleteDataset.Clone, GetClauses, Expression, ReturnsColumns, GetAs, exp.SelectClauses, exp.NewSelectClauses, exp.InsertClauses, exp.NewInsertClauses, exp.UpdateClauses, exp.NewUpdateClauses, exp.DeleteClauses, exp.NewDeleteClauses, exp.Expression, exp.ColumnListExpression, exp.NewColumnListExpression, exp.ArrayExpression, exp.NewArrayExpression, exp.Distinctable, exp.Comparable, exp.Inable, exp.Isable, exp.Likeable, exp.Rangeable, exp.Orderable, exp.Castable, exp.Updateable: the inner clauses and the interfaces a dataset is made of; every value here is a copy, so a query is copied by `=` and its fields read by name
  go      goqu.SetTimeLocation, goqu.SetColumnRenameFunction, goqu.SetIgnoreUntaggedFields, goqu.Logger, squirrel.NoContextSupport, squirrel.RunnerNotQueryRunner, squirrel.RunnerNotSet: settings of a package-wide mutable global, which the language refuses, and errors of running
  python  sqlalchemy.inspect, sqlalchemy.event, sqlalchemy.engine, sqlalchemy.pool, sqlalchemy.exc: the engine, its events and its pool, which are a connection's and stand in `sql/postgres` and `sql/sqlite`
